date_type = 1
edits_description = "The image was cropped and text overlays were removed."
final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_b7kdy")
province = 71
blurb = "Depicts a water wheel which carries water into a wooden flume that cuts horizontally across the foreground. Two farmers carry sacks of unhulled rice. Women are washing hulled rice in the water of the flume. A little boy, bored, leads his pet turtle on a string to the water. Hokusai is contrasting the activities of people completely absorbed in their task with Mount Fuji, remote and untouched.

Such mills for hulling rice were powered by the waters of the Shibuya River in Onden. Located between Harajuku and Aoyama, now one of the posh centers of Tōkyō, Onden was still a sparsely populated rural area in Hokusai's time."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
